      "interviewQuestions": [
        "Explain how LB vs Reverse Proxy impacts the trade-off between consistency and availability during network splits.",
        "What are the typical hardware resource limits (e.g. disk write operations, bandwidth, thread pools) when scaling LB vs Reverse Proxy?"
      ],
      "summary": "In summary, LB vs Reverse Proxy offers a robust, industry-standard pattern for scaling distributed systems. By decoupling responsibilities, managing coordination overheads, and planning for hardware fault zones, developers can build resilient services that handle millions of active clients."
